    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "4 Anglers Rest is a very well-located two-bedroom townhouse, quietly positioned within a small gated development close to Donnybrook Village, with the amenities of Ballsbridge, Ranelagh and Clonskeagh, UCD and the beautiful Dodder River Greenway all within easy reach.\r\nExtending to approximately 66 sq. m. (710 sq. ft.), No. 4 is particularly well positioned within the development, on the gated courtyard side accessed from Beech Hill Avenue. The property enjoys an excellent south-easterly orientation, which, combined with its three-level layout and generous windows, creates a notably bright and uplifting interior with good natural light throughout the day.\r\nThe accommodation is thoughtfully arranged over three levels. The ground floor comprises an entrance hall and main bedroom with en-suite, together with useful under-stairs storage incorporating plumbing for a washing machine. The first floor provides a bright and spacious open-plan kitchen/living area, with the modern kitchen neatly positioned within an alcove, creating defined areas for cooking, dining and relaxing. The second floor completes the accommodation with a second double bedroom with fitted wardrobes, a hot press and a generous main bathroom.\r\nWell-presented throughout, with the benefit of modern kitchen and bathroom fittings, this attractive townhouse combines bright, well-proportioned accommodation with an excellent location. It is likely to appeal to a wide range of purchasers, including first-time buyers, those looking to downsize and anyone seeking a conveniently located Dublin base. Further benefits include its own private entrance and a secure designated car parking space.\r\nLocated on Beaver Row alongside the River Dodder, No. 4 occupies a particularly pleasant position at the entrance to Anglers Rest. The development is privately gated and comprises just 19 own-door residential units. The nearby Dodder River Greenway provides an especially attractive amenity, with its riverside walks and green open spaces offering an excellent opportunity for walking, running and cycling practically on the doorstep.\r\nThe property is also within easy reach of Donnybrook and Ranelagh villages, offering an excellent choice of cafés, restaurants, shops and everyday amenities. Other nearby facilities include David Lloyd Dublin Riverview and Richview Business Park. The city centre is well served by frequent bus routes, while Herbert Park, the RDS Arena, University College Dublin and the Aviva Stadium are all within easy reach, providing excellent connectivity to the city and surrounding areas."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Ground Floor \r\nEntrance Hall (5.74m x 0.99m): Under-stairs storage incorporating plumbing for a washing machine.\r\nBedroom 2 (4.02m x 2.58m): Double bedroom with hardwood flooring and En-Suite (1.62m x 1.76m) fully tiled, with shower, w.c.,and w.h.b\r\n\r\nFirst Floor\r\nLanding (2.43m x 1.74m) \r\nLiving Room (3.86m x 3.67m) : Bright and spacious living area with laminate flooring\r\nKitchen (2.53m x 1.83m) :  Fitted with floor and wall units and a tiled splashback \r\n\r\nSecond Floor \r\nLanding (2.43m x 1.74m) \r\nBedroom 1 (3.30m x 3.67m) : Double bedroom with hardwood flooring and fitted wardrobes\r\nBathroom (2.40m x 1.83m) : Tiled Bathroom with bath, w.c. and w.h.b."
      },
